===1996 election===
The 1996 election, the first under the new electoral system [[Mixed-member proportional|MMP]], saw ACT candidate and former Labour Cabinet Minister [[Richard Prebble]] compete against former National Party [[Wellington-Karori]] MP [[Pauline Gardiner]] now standing for [[United New Zealand]], the National party candidate Mark Thomas, Labour's Alick Shaw and Danna Glendining for the Alliance.

The election campaign saw Prime Minister [[Jim Bolger]] endorse Richard Prebble shortly before the election in preference to Thomas. The events were captured in the movie Campaign.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nzonscreen.com/title/campaign|title=Campaign – Film – NZ On Screen|website=Nzonscreen.com|access-date=17 September 2017}}</ref> The electorate was won by Richard Prebble.<ref name="auto">{{cite web|url=http://www.electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_1996/pdf/6.1%20Wellington%20Central%2056.pdf|title=Wellington 56|website=Electionresults.govt.nz|access-date=17 September 2017}}</ref>

